agent-bridge project bootstrap

Read `PROJECT_MAP.md` first. It is the canonical quick-memory map for this repository.

Use `README.md` for user-facing usage and `docs/architecture.md` for deeper reference, but treat `PROJECT_MAP.md` as the operational summary of the current implementation.

Critical hotspots:
- `src/registry/server.ts`: central registry, WS events, channel endpoints
- `src/agent/server.ts`: agent runtime, A2A/JSON-RPC, AG-UI SSE, registry registration
- `src/agent/handlers.ts`: task lifecycle, skill routing, default RPC methods
- `src/mcp/adapter.ts`: MCP bridge, client-session messaging, inbox-first behavior
- `dashboard/src/stores/*`: registry, trace, and chat state in the UI

Current reality to remember:
- Local-first system on `localhost`
- Registry agent state is in memory; channel conversations persist in `.agent-bridge/registry.sqlite`
- A2A streaming is partial; AG-UI SSE exists
- No meaningful automated test suite; validation is mainly builds and manual flows
